  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "In 1419, a clockmaker named Filippo Brunelleschi started work on a very difficult project."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "He was building the dome of Florence’s main cathedral, 1 the Basilica di Santa Maria del Fiore."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "For 1,500 years, the world’s largest dome belonged to the Pantheon in Rome."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Brunelleschi’s job was to build one even larger."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "The building of the cathedral began in 1296."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "By 1359, much of it was complete, but no one knew how to build its dome."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "Many builders could build concrete 2 domes."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "However, the dome in Florence needed to be wider than any dome ever built."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "A concrete dome would be too heavy and would easily fall."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "The cathedral, therefore, remained unfinished for many years."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Filippo Brunelleschi promised to find a solution."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "He said he would build two domes, an inner dome made of stone and an outer one made of light bricks."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "3 He would use lighter materials as he worked upwards."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "Strong rings made of stone, wood, and iron would hold everything together."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "Do we understand how it was built?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "Brunelleschi also had to find a way to lift the materials high into the air."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "What did he do?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "He invented a new machine to do the job."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "Building the dome took 16 years."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "Brunelleschi had done something no one else could."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "However, he left no pictures of his design."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "So—even today—experts don’t fully understand how this incredible structure was built."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
